cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use CNS Rover in your work, please cite this software. See
  ATTRIBUTION.md for the separate credits and licenses of the MaleCNS
  dataset and other upstream assets.
title: "CNS Rover"
abstract: >-
  A Python robot-car simulator and browser workbench for connectome-guided
  navigation. The native controller combines an independently extracted
  MaleCNS v1.0 neural circuit and a freshly trained car readout with
  RGB-based obstacle avoidance, target tracking, and braking. Controllers
  receive camera pixels and simulated time, without access to simulator
  ground truth. The workbench supports scenario editing, controller
  comparisons, visual-input ablation, telemetry, deterministic recording,
  and replay. The system is an experimental reduced-circuit simulation
  with engineered perception and control, without biological validation
  or demonstrated real-robot safety guarantees.
type: software
